📅 Day 50 – Request & Response Handling in Servlets

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on handling client-server communication using request and response objects in servlets. The mentor explained how data is received from the client and how responses are sent back dynamically.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Request Object (HttpServletRequest)
Used to receive data from the client (browser)
Retrieves form data using methods like:
getParameter()
getParameterValues()
Stores information about the request
2️⃣ Response Object (HttpServletResponse)
Used to send output back to the client
Generates dynamic content (HTML response)
Uses PrintWriter to display output
3️⃣ Client-Server Communication Flow
Client sends request (form data)
Servlet receives request using request object
Data is processed on server
Response is sent back to client
🔹 Practical Work

During the practice session, I:

Created forms to collect user input
Used request object to extract parameters
Processed input data in servlet
Used response object to display results dynamically

This helped me understand how data flows between the client and server in real-time applications.